===persian===

جنگ تمام شد...
و... تو ادامه داری...
و جنگل هنوز پای‌بند دریاست...
و من تو را دوست دارم... که
هر روز
خواهش محجوب جنگل را
برهنه،
به دریا می‌گویی...

اسفند ۱۳۶۷

===machine===

The war ended...
And... you continue...
And the jungle is still bound to the sea...
And I love you... because
Every day
You nakedly tell
The modest desire of the jungle
To the sea...

Esfand 1367

===lantern===

The war is over...
and... you go on...
and the forest is still bound to the sea...
and I love you... because
every day
the forest's bashful longing
you speak — naked —
to the sea...

Esfand 1367

===translation===

The war has ended...
and... you go on...
and still the forest is bound to the sea...
and I love you... because, every day,
the bashful longing of the forest
you tell — naked —
to the sea...

— Esfand 1367

===footnotes===

Companion to the page-61 poem: the sea/forest pair returns, now as a figure for the lovers. پای‌بند is "bound, pledged, faithful to." خواهش محجوب is the "bashful / modest desire" of the forest, which the beloved speaks برهنه (nakedly, openly) to the sea — she is the one who says aloud, without shame, the longing the forest cannot. Esfand is the last month of the Persian year (Feb–Mar 1989); the Iran–Iraq ceasefire had taken hold the previous summer, so "the war has ended" is literal as well as figurative.
